  "title": "India's Strategic Steel Policy and Economic Growth",
  "summary": "The Indian government has announced a new steel policy aiming to boost India's crude steel capacity to 604 million tonnes by 2047, enhancing industry competitiveness and addressing import challenges. The policy will increase finished steel demand to 505 million tonnes by 2047, with per capita consumption set at 302 kg and steel exports at 45 million tonnes. Raw materials such as iron ore, coking coal, and manganese will be prioritized to reduce reliance on imports and improve resource sustainability.",
